      "problem": "Evaluate $(\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{20}{16})$ means the same thing as ${}_{20}{C}_{16}.$\n\n In general, the number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=20$ and $r=16,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{20}{C}_{16} & =\\frac{20!}{(20-16)!16!} \\\\  & =\\frac{20!}{4!16!} \\\\  & =\\frac{20\\cdot 19\\cdot 18\\cdot 17\\cdot \\cancel{16!}}{4!\\cancel{16!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{20\\cdot 19\\cdot 18\\cdot 17}{4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{116\\,280}{24} \\\\  & =4\\,845.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
